GLOSSARY = [
    ["PropNEAT", "NEAT (NeuroEvolution of Augmenting Topologies) with backpropagation: evolution searches the topology, and each generation the genomes' weights are trained by gradient descent (a set number of backprop epochs per generation).", "project developer guide (repo root) (project overview, `backproppop.py`)"],
    ["Best-by-train selection", "The genome reported for a run is the one with the best training fitness over the run; the test split is never used to select (only logged).", "thesis/notes/THESIS_EXPERIMENTS.md (1.2, 1.7); experiments/mnist/README.md"],
    ["Support", "The points the model was trained on. Equivalence between models is only ever established there.", "docs/signals-and-realisations/README.md §2"],
    ["Signal", "A function of the inputs that the model uses, identified on the support; in practice, the contribution of one leaf annotation. In the proposition: a component f_S of the Bayes predictor's functional ANOVA decomposition with strength ‖f_S‖² > 0.", "docs/signals-and-realisations/README.md §2, §3a"],
    ["Realisation", "A subgraph, with its weights and activation function, that computes a signal. Two realisations of the same signal agree on the support and can disagree between and beyond the training points.", "docs/signals-and-realisations/README.md §2"],
    ["Alias", "Two realisations of the same signal, in different runs or within one network.", "docs/signals-and-realisations/README.md §2"],
    ["Family", "A set of realisations of a signal between which you can move continuously without the signal changing on the support (counted up to symmetries that keep the mechanism).", "docs/signals-and-realisations/README.md §2"],
    ["Cell", "Within a family, which training points fall on the active side of each unit's fold; explanations tend to name cells (\"AND gate\", \"single-input hinge\").", "docs/signals-and-realisations/README.md §2"],
    ["Equivalence levels E0–E3", "Two models are equivalent at E0 if they make the same decisions on the support, E1 the same scores on the support, E2 the same family for each signal, E3 the same function everywhere.", "docs/signals-and-realisations/README.md §2"],
    ["Annotation", "A subgraph hypothesis A = (entry nodes, exit nodes, nodes, connections, hypothesis, evidence): it declares that the subgraph computes its exits as a function F of its entries.", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md (Annotation); docs/theoretical_framework.md"],
    ["Leaf", "An annotation with no children: it explains a primitive subgraph in isolation.", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md (Annotation types)"],
    ["Composition", "An annotation that explains how its child annotations combine, e.g. F(a,b,c) = G(a,b) + H(b,c) (parallel) or H(G(a,b), c) (serial).", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md; docs/theoretical_framework.md"],
    ["Part", "The annotation a hidden unit belongs to: the smallest annotation that holds a copy of it as a non-entry node (`part_of`).", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md (Depth is not penalised)"],
    ["Root", "The global root: the single annotation with no parent whose expanded subgraph contains every output node, and from which every other annotation descends.", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md (Compositional coverage)"],
    ["Structural coverage", "The fraction of model nodes covered by the leaf annotations (Null parts count as covered).", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md (Structural coverage)"],
    ["Compositional coverage", "Present / required composition steps; equals 1 if and only if there is exactly one root, it reaches every output, and every annotation descends from it.", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md (Compositional coverage)"],
    ["Full coverage / well-formed", "Structural and compositional coverage both 1.0, all leaves valid, and the root covers the whole model.", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md (Well-formed explanation)"],
    ["Null explanation", "Anything shown to have zero effect on the result has the trivial explanation Null. **Exact Null** (no path to an output over enabled non-zero edges; zero-weight edges) is automatic, counts as covered and is exempt from the single-root rule. **Support-level Null** (e.g. a unit never active on the data) needs an evidenced Null annotation.", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md (Null explanations)"],
    ["Split node", "An identity operation: a node with several roles is replaced by copies (`5_a`, `5_b`, …), each carrying one outgoing connection and all the original incoming ones, so the roles can sit in different annotations without changing the function.", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md (Node splitting); project developer guide (repo root)"],
    ["Identity node", "An identity operation: a pass-through node inserted to intercept connections (e.g. when an exit has external inputs), making a subgraph annotatable without changing the function.", "project developer guide (repo root) (Annotation strategy)"],
    ["Faithful", "Level 1: the hierarchy computes the model's function (by construction, since the refactoring operations are identity operations; tested by the closed-form errors).", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md (Three levels)"],
    ["Decomposed", "Level 2: each leaf is a small, separately readable part (leaf count, granularity, the swallowed-layer warning).", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md (Three levels)"],
    ["Understood", "Level 3: each leaf maps to a concept a domain reader recognises. Measured by Mike's leaf verdict (understood / partial / not); the concept probe, ground-truth recovery and the blind verifier's leaf grades are automated screens.", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md (Who decides \"understood\")"],
    ["Granularity", "The share of hidden units whose part has width ≤ 6 (width = the most hidden units in one layer of the part). A whole wide layer in one leaf is \"covered, not decomposed\".", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md (Depth is not penalised)"],
    ["Concept probe (v1 / v2)", "Scores how well a named concept predicts a leaf's exit (score = max(R², 2(AUC − 0.5)) where AUC may count): meaningful ≥ 0.8, partial ≥ 0.5, else closed-form only. **v2** (13 Nov) adds two conditions: simplicity (a concept that merely reweights the leaf's own entries is a `restatement`) and support (a binary concept needs ≥ 1% minority share; AUC counts only for a gate of comparable support). v1 lacked both.", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md (The concept probe; probe v2)"],
    ["Meaningful / partial / closed-form only", "The probe's grades for a leaf: a named concept predicts it well, moderately, or not at all (the leaf is described only by its formula).", "docs/annotation_coverage_model.md (The concept probe)"],
    ["Blind verifier", "An independent agent that challenges an explanation from the record alone at four levels (L1 mechanical re-check, L2 evidential, L3 adversarial probing, L4 domain sense).", "explanation-verifier skill description"],
    ["Upheld / weakened / refuted", "The verifier's grade for each claim or part: it stands; it holds only in a narrower form (scope, wording, a number); or it is shown false with concrete inputs and numbers.", "explanation-verifier skill description; experiments/explanation_barrier/RESULTS.md"],
    ["Recheck", "`explaneat verify recheck`: re-checks a record's numbers and their provenance against the live model; reports `mismatch` only when confident, else `needs_review`.", "project developer guide (repo root) (MCP server)"],
    ["Provenance", "Every evidence and query result is logged in `evidence_log` with tool, arguments, population, quantity, scope, split, n and a rows hash; narratives cite numbers as references `{{q:<id>.<path>}}` rather than typing them.", "project developer guide (repo root) (MCP server)"],
    ["Strict mode", "Explanation integrity on: bare typed numbers and \"exact\" formulas that do not reproduce are refused when written.", "project developer guide (repo root) (MCP server)"],
    ["Rashomon set", "The ε-Rashomon set R(ε) = { g : L(g) ≤ L* + ε }. Thesis convention: within the PropNEAT class, relative to the best observed seed, ε = 0.01 in test AUC.", "docs/signals-and-realisations/README.md §3, §3a"],
    ["Mandatory / optional signal", "Under the proposition, a signal stronger than ε must be realised by every member of R(ε); weaker ones may be dropped.", "docs/signals-and-realisations/README.md §3a"],
    ["Signoff-v1", "The protocol by which Mike verifies a v4 record and records `mike_verification` (a PREREG amendment of 11 Nov); a protocol name, not a git tag.", "thesis/notes/THESIS_EXPERIMENTS.md §2.4"],
]
